                          \ ==== Break: Ctrl-Break and Ctrl-C (doc/vm.md, section 9) ===============
                          \ The BIOS calls INT 1Bh for Ctrl-Break at once, also in a loop of Forth;
                          \ DOS calls INT 23h when it sees Ctrl-C at the console. Both handlers
                          \ only change the table: each primitive is BREAK now. So the next
                          \ primitive runs BREAK, where the VM is complete, and NEXT costs nothing
                          \ more. BREAK puts the table back. While DOS reads a line of the
                          \ keyboard (WAITING), Ctrl-C only gives the prompt again; DOS then reads
                          \ the line again.
                          
                          FORWARD BREAK
                          LABEL BREAK-ON   \ each primitive is BREAK now; keeps all registers
1000  50 51 57 06           AX PUSH,  CX PUSH,  DI PUSH,  ES PUSH,
1004  0E 07 BF 03 01 B8     CS PUSH,  ES POP,  DI OPTAB MOVI,  AX BREAK MOVI,  CX 128 MOVI,  CLD,  REP, STOSW,
100A  4A 10 B9 80 00 FC
1010  F3 AB
1012  2E C7 06 4B 07 01     CS: BRK-FLAG [] 1 MOVI,
1018  00
1019  07 5F 59 58 C3        ES POP,  DI POP,  CX POP,  AX POP,  RET,
                          LABEL ON-1B      \ INT 1Bh: Ctrl-Break
101E  2E 83 3E 49 07 00     CS: WAITING [] 0 CMPI,  Z IF,  BREAK-ON CALL,  THEN,  IRET,
1024  75 03 E8 D7 FF CF
                          LABEL ON-23      \ INT 23h: Ctrl-C, seen by DOS; an IRET makes DOS go on
102A  2E 83 3E 49 07 00     CS: WAITING [] 0 CMPI,  Z IF,  BREAK-ON CALL,  IRET,  THEN,
1030  75 04 E8 CB FF CF
1036  50 53 51 52           AX PUSH,  BX PUSH,  CX PUSH,  DX PUSH,
103A  2E 8B 0E 51 07 BA     CS: CX OUT-LEN [] MOV,  DX OUT-BUF MOVI,  WRITE-CS CALL,   \ the prompt again
1040  00 F2 E8 1A F9
1045  5A 59 5B 58 CF        DX POP,  CX POP,  BX POP,  AX POP,  IRET,
                          LABEL BREAK      \ in the place of a primitive: stop the running word
104A  1E 06 0E 1F 0E 07     DS PUSH,  ES PUSH,  CS PUSH,  DS POP,  CS PUSH,  ES POP,
1050  BE 00 F5 BF 03 01     SI OPTAB0 MOVI,  DI OPTAB MOVI,  CX 128 MOVI,  REP, MOVSW,   \ the table back
