                          \ ==== The console: primitives 29-31 =====================================
                          \ ?RX gives the characters of LINE-BUF. A new line comes when QUIT waits
                          \ in REFILL; a word that reads keys gets "no key" while files load, or
                          \ when the input is a file. At the keyboard, KEY? does not wait: DOS
                          \ tells if a key is there (0Bh); then DOS reads the whole line.
                          
                          29 CODE ?RX
109D  2E A1 4D 07 2E 3B     CS: AX IN-POS [] MOV,  CS: AX IN-LEN [] CMP,  L1 JB,     \ a character of the line is there
10A3  06 4F 07 72 2B
10A8  E8 6B FA 72 23        REFILLING CALL,  L2 JC,                                  \ QUIT waits for a line
10AD  2E 83 3E 59 07 00     CS: CUR-FID [] 0 CMPI,  L3 JNZ,                          \ a file loads: no key
10B3  75 3F
10B5  2E A1 57 07 2E 3B     CS: AX ARGI [] MOV,  CS: AX NARGS [] CMP,  L3 JB,        \ files wait: no key
10BB  06 55 07 72 34
10C0  2E 83 3E 47 07 00     CS: TTY [] 0 CMPI,  L3 JZ,                               \ input from a file: no key
10C6  74 2C
10C8  B4 0B CD 21 08 C0     $0B DOS,  AL AL OR,  L3 JZ,                              \ no key yet
10CE  74 24
                          LABEL L2
10D0  E8 75 FE              NEXT-LINE CALL,
